Subject: [PATCH] feat: CCTV module gets Overview -> Map -> Equipment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

First of the four modules Marcelo specified a common shape for: a
summary landing page, then the module's own GIS map, then the
equipment list you click through to edit. CCTV had none of this — it
was a single table with no map at all.

- CamerasPageClient.tsx (new): Overview | Map | Equipment tabs.
  Overview summarises counts, how many are placed on the map, and the
  status / communication / power / model mix (models read from the
  camera_models catalog). Clicking a row in Equipment opens that camera
  on the Map with its editor already open — the same
  jump-to-with-focus pattern NetworkPageClient already uses, so there
  is one camera editor rather than two that can drift.
- ProjectMapCanvas: three optional props — moduleScope, focusCameraId,
  onFocusHandled. With moduleScope="cctv" the fiber and network
  overlays start switched off so the module map shows its own
  discipline (they can still be turned on as reference). Every prop is
  optional and defaults to today's behaviour, so the combined project
  map the client is currently looking at is untouched.
- cameras/page.tsx: renders the client shell and also loads network
  devices, which the map component needs to mount.

